  "revisionModel": {
    "assessmentRevision": "Monotonic counter over assessed facts. Increments when a bound field, the evidence set, the review disposition of evidence, or the requirement set changes. Does NOT increment on decision.recorded, because a decision records an opinion about facts and does not alter them.",
    "eventSequence": "Monotonic counter over every appended event, including decision.recorded.",
    "decisionBinding": "A decision stores targetAssessmentRevision, requirementSetVersion, requirementSetDigest and evidenceSetDigest. It is current iff targetAssessmentRevision equals the current assessmentRevision AND requirementSetVersion matches AND every evidence record in evidenceSetDigest remains accepted and unexpired.",
    "why": "Binding a decision to the event sequence would stale it the instant it is written, because writing it advances that sequence. Binding it to the assessed facts keeps a decision current until a fact actually changes."
  },

